<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10440" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">con-sĕco</span></b> , cŭi, ctum,
		1, v. a. (rare; not in Cic.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To cut up, cut to pieces</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">brassicam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 157</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nasturtium minutatim,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 10, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rapa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1, 59, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">membra fratris (Medea),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 3, 9, 34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genas,</span>”
				<i>to lacerate</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 137, 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			Pliny, <i>to cut off, lop, prune</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">surculos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					12, 19, 43, § 96</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">truncum arboris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					17, 10, 9, § 58</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">36, 26, 66,
				§ 193</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
